Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New /admin/leads page, its own nav item (separate from Commercial
Accounts, which is signed-up billing customers — leads are just
prospects). Admin enters a free-text category (spas, gyms, Airbnb
property managers, mom groups, whatever) and a geographic area, plus a
result count (3-20). This calls ScrapeGraphAI's searchScraper API
server-side with a structured output_schema so results come back as
clean business_name/contact_name/email/phone/website/service_area
fields instead of prose to parse.

searchScraper is async (POST returns a request_id in queued/processing
state), so app/actions/leads.ts stores that request_id and the admin UI
polls checkLeadSearchStatus() client-side every few seconds rather than
holding one serverless invocation open for the 60-90+ seconds these
searches have taken in manual testing.

New tables (migration already applied directly via Supabase MCP, not
included in this diff since there's no local migrations/ folder in this
repo): lead_searches (one row per search, tracks status/request_id) and
commercial_leads (one row per extracted lead, FK to the search it came
from). Followed the app's existing convention of no RLS — access
controlled entirely through requireAdmin()-gated server actions, same as
every other table.

Requires SGAI_API_KEY as a Vercel env var — not set yet, needs to be
added before this works in production.
